{"title":"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of equilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245ff420d808b2e09a77194551ff12dbfda05a19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABE}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is in the interior of unit square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the region consisting of all points inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and outside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245ff420d808b2e09a77194551ff12dbfda05a19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABE}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> whose distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. What is the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46ae55588d82d574ce8f6641b183151e0c39892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{12-5\\sqrt3}{72} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{12-5\\sqrt3}{36} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt3}{18} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{3-\\sqrt3}{9} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{\\sqrt3}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"573\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The region is the shaded area:\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c138ff4f242efb62680b69d5db830a4762be1b42.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D,E; A=(0,1); B=(1,1); C=(1,0); D=(0,0); E=(1/2,1-sqrt(3)/2); draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,NW); dot(A); label(&quot;B&quot;,B,NE); dot(B); label(&quot;C&quot;,C,SE); dot(C); label(&quot;D&quot;,D,SW); dot(D); draw(A--E--B--cycle); label(&quot;E&quot;,E,S); dot(E); draw((1/3,0)--(1/3,1)); draw((2/3,0)--(2/3,1)); fill((1/3,0)--(1/3,1-sqrt(3)/3)--E--(2/3,1-sqrt(3)/3)--(2/3,0)--cycle,Black);[/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"248\" />\n</center>\n<p>We can find the area of the shaded region by subtracting the pentagon from the middle third of the square.  The area of the middle third of the square is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a6a945fea92dad88830947871c74ffe9c9c54db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac13\\right)(1)=\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"101\" height=\"43\" />.  The pentagon can be split into a rectangle and an equilateral triangle.\n</p><p>The base of the equilateral triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebafcc60a28d8759185d7808c60ea53efc73938e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d43c3b121f052fbd6bdff8e00b2c0d1869e7c5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac13\\right)\\left(\\frac12\\right)(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"174\" height=\"45\" />.  Thus, the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/8/038472e937aeb576b47ab90b60827e5e3f9ce86c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{6}\\right)\\left(\\frac13\\right)\\left(\\frac12\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"192\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>The base of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/a/ebafcc60a28d8759185d7808c60ea53efc73938e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> and the height is the height of the equilateral triangle minus the height of the smaller equilateral triangle.  This is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06cd3ac5b3221a4286dccf7628dff86254acd51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{6}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"133\" height=\"43\" />\nTherefore, the area of the shaded region is\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cb577d918454570f76d3849dc7774824a1ba4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac13-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{9}-\\frac{\\sqrt3}{36}=\\boxed{\\text{(B) }\\frac{12-5\\sqrt3}{36}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"261\" height=\"53\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B\">2008 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AMC_12B_Pr